THE GAP I LEFT IN THM-1350: det JF const bounds only the PRODUCT of blocks.
sigma acts as (-1,-1,+1), so on Fix(sigma)={x=y=0} the tangent space splits:
  +1 eigenspace = z-direction (tangent to Fix);  -1 eigenspace = (x,y)-plane.

J at (0,0,z):
[ 0   0  1]
[         ]
[3*z  1  0]
[         ]
[ 2   0  0]

  tangential determinant (d/dz of F|Fix) = 1
  normal 2x2 block det at (0,0,z)        = -2
  product = -2   det JF = -2

THE REPAIR (the argument I should have written):
  On Fix, det JF = det(tangential) * det(normal), both POLYNOMIALS in z.
  Their product is the nonzero constant -2.  In the domain C[z], a product
  of polynomials equal to a nonzero constant forces EACH factor to be a
  nonzero constant (degrees add).  Hence the tangential block is a nonzero
  constant, i.e. F|Fix IS Keller in dimension dim Fix(sigma).  The claim
  stands; the proof needed this step.

  check both are constants here: tangential 1 (deg 0? 0), normal -2 (deg 0? 0)
